Design a production-grade, multi-tenant User Service API using FastAPI and Supabase.

Architecture Requirements:
- Follow clean architecture:
  - API Layer (FastAPI routers)
  - Service Layer (business logic)
  - Repository Layer (Supabase/PostgreSQL access)
- Dependency injection for services and auth
- Modular design for testability and scalability

Multi-Tenancy Model:
- Support multi-tenant SaaS architecture
- Entities:
  - Tenant (id, name, status)
  - User (id, tenant_id, email, full_name, status)
  - Membership (user_id, tenant_id, role_id)
- Enforce tenant isolation at all layers
- All queries must be tenant-scoped
- Support tenant-level configuration

RBAC + Permissions:
- Role-based access control with fine-grained permissions
- Entities:
  - Role (id, name, tenant_id)
  - Permission (id, resource, action)
  - RolePermission mapping
- Support:
  - System roles (global)
  - Tenant roles (scoped)
- Authorization:
  - JWT-based (Supabase Auth)
  - Middleware/dependencies to enforce permissions
- Example permissions:
  - user.read, user.write, user.delete, tenant.admin

API Endpoints:
- Auth:
  - POST /auth/signup
  - POST /auth/login
  - GET /auth/me
- Tenants:
  - POST /tenants
  - GET /tenants/{id}
- Users:
  - POST /users
  - GET /users/{id}
  - GET /users (filter by tenant, role, status)
  - PUT /users/{id}
  - DELETE /users/{id} (soft delete)
- Roles & Permissions:
  - CRUD /roles
  - CRUD /permissions
  - Assign roles to users

Data & Schema:
- PostgreSQL (Supabase) schema design
- UUID primary keys
- Audit fields:
  - created_at, updated_at
  - created_by, updated_by
- Soft delete:
  - deleted_at (nullable)
- Indexing strategy for multi-tenant queries

Audit & Compliance:
- Full audit trail for:
  - user changes
  - role/permission changes
  - authentication events
- Audit log schema:
  - id, actor_id, action, resource, resource_id, timestamp, metadata
- Support compliance requirements:
  - GDPR (data access & deletion)
  - Immutable audit logs
- Track:
  - who did what, when, and from where (IP optional)

Security:
- Supabase JWT authentication
- Row-Level Security (RLS) policies for tenant isolation
- Input validation (Pydantic)
- OWASP best practices
- Rate limiting
- Secrets management (no hardcoded secrets)

Error Handling:
- Standard error model:
  - code, message, details, trace_id
- Consistent HTTP status usage
- Validation vs business logic errors separation

Testability (SDET-focused):
- API must be test-friendly:
  - Deterministic responses
  - Idempotent endpoints where applicable
- Include:
  - Test scenarios for each endpoint
  - Mocking strategy for Supabase
  - Dependency override patterns (FastAPI)
- Define:
  - Unit tests (service layer)
  - Integration tests (API + DB)
  - Contract tests (OpenAPI validation)
- Provide sample test cases:
  - Auth flows
  - RBAC enforcement
  - Tenant isolation
- Include test data seeding strategy

Observability:
- Structured logging (JSON)
- Correlation/trace IDs
- Metrics hooks (latency, error rates)
- Audit logs integration

Performance & Scalability:
- Pagination (cursor-based preferred)
- Filtering and sorting
- Indexing recommendations
- Avoid N+1 queries
- Async support (FastAPI)

Output Requirements:
1. OpenAPI 3.0 specification (YAML)
2. Pydantic models (request/response)
3. Suggested FastAPI folder structure
4. Supabase/PostgreSQL schema (DDL)
5. Example RLS policies
6. Example middleware/dependencies (auth + RBAC)
7. Sample test cases (pytest style)
8. Example audit log entries

Constraints:
- No sensitive data in API responses
- Passwords must be handled only via Supabase Auth
- All endpoints must enforce tenant context